In the above program, if statement is with (;) at the end. (;) at the end of if statement indicates empty body of if block. Therefore above program can be rewritten as #include <stdio.h> 
int main()
{
    int a = 2;
    if(a == 5)
    {//empty body of if due to (;)
    }
    {
        printf("Mock Test ");
    }
    printf("practicepaper.in");
    return 0;
} In this code, both printf statements always executes irrespective of condition becomes true or false. OUTPUT : Mock Test practicepaper.in

